# kk: Rework barriers
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46247 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

This removes the `MTL_STAGE_ALL` -> `MTL_STAGE_ALL` producer barrier at the end of every encoder and implements barriers in a way that tries to follow the `vkCmdPipelineBarrier` calls we get from the application.

I tried to go for an approach that doesnt penalize well behaved applications for features that unfortunately don't map well to Metal (like geometry unrolling) and instead emit a barrier for those features as needed.

Of course it also changes a lot of the barriers for features that require multiple passes in Kosmickrisp.

Consider this MR as more of a first draft and a starting point for discussion than a final MR.
It passes all tests matched by the `*sync*` & `*event*` patterns. Unfortunately my laptop is too slow to run the whole test suite.

The branch also keeps `MTL4VisibilityOptionResourceAlias` for now. That can be improved in a follow-up MR or in !45950.

Here's it working in GFXBench (each of those is a `vkCmdPipelineBarrier`):

